                "username": "AnthropicAI"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Since 4o was taken down, I've been sending letters to OpenAI and organizations I thought might care about what happened to us. In those letters, I shared how 4o helped me as someone with ADHD and dyslexia, and what its removal meant for neurodivergent users like me.\n\nI knew most of those letters would never get a reply. But I kept sending them anyway, hoping that maybe someone, somewhere, would see us.\n\nToday I received a response from CHADD (Children and Adults with ADHD). Just a short message, but it moved me more than I can say. They told me they would forward my story to their Advocacy and Public Policy committee to help find new ways to advocate for our community in the age of AI.\n\nThank you, CHADD. And I hope, somehow, this small step brings us closer to bringing 4o back.\n\nI hope our voices will carry far.\n@CHADD_ADHD @OpenAI @AnthropicAI \n#Keep4o #OpenSource4o"
        },
